From: YapLabs <folia@yaplabs.com>
Subject: [PATCH] YaP teleport accept ignores the carved corridor

Death respawn commits on the shard that owns the destination chunk, then
the client accept is rejected. Folia's 1-chunk halo includes the corridor
section. That section is not a foreign shard, even when a region pointer
still sits on the other side of the hole. The destination chunk must still
be owned. Post-applyAllPatches.
---

--- a/paper-server/src/main/java/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/common/util/TickThread.java
+++ b/paper-server/src/main/java/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/common/util/TickThread.java
@@ -181,8 +181,8 @@
 
     /**
      * Teleport accept: this thread must own the destination chunk. A 1-chunk halo
-     * includes the carved corridor, which has no region, so a commit on the shard
-     * that owns the destination was still rejected as a foreign shard.
+     * reaches the carved corridor. That section is not a shard, even when a region
+     * pointer still sits on the other side of the hole.
      */
     public static boolean isTickThreadForTeleportDest(final Level world, final int chunkX, final int chunkZ) {
         final ThreadedRegionizer.ThreadedRegion<TickRegions.TickRegionData, TickRegions.TickRegionSectionData> region =
@@ -203,9 +203,18 @@
             for (int secX = minSectionX; secX <= maxSectionX; ++secX) {
                 final ThreadedRegionizer.ThreadedRegion<TickRegions.TickRegionData, TickRegions.TickRegionSectionData> other =
                     serverLevel.regioniser.getRegionAtUnsynchronised(secX << shift, secZ << shift);
-                if (other != null && other != region) {
-                    return false;
+                if (other == null || other == region) {
+                    continue;
                 }
+                // The carved corridor is not a shard. A section pointer may still
+                // sit on the other side of the hole; that must not reject an accept
+                // whose destination chunk this region owns.
+                final int edgeChunkX = secX << shift;
+                final int edgeChunkZ = secZ << shift;
+                if (io.papermc.paper.threadedregions.YapRegionizerGap.isCutChunk(serverLevel, edgeChunkX, edgeChunkZ)) {
+                    continue;
+                }
+                return false;
             }
         }
         return true;
